  "report_period": "Week 49 (29th Nov to 6th Dec 2024)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "SK Shipping have committed their Capesize \"K. Victory\" 181/2012 Sasebo, Japan (SS 07/2027, DD 07/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) to undisclosed interests at USD 33,5 mill and the one-year-younger sister vessel \"K. Confidence\" 181/2013 Sasebo, Japan (SS 01/2028, DD 10/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) to clients of Chinaland Shipping at USD 34,5 mill. Remind you that the \"Sea Triumph\" 181/2012 Koyo, Japan (SS 02/2027, DD 01/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold in late July at USD 36 mill. Furthermore, Japanese owners committed the \"Cape Dream\" 179/2011 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 06/2026, BWTS fitted) at USD 28 mill, while the sister vessel \"Cape Keystone\" 179/2011 Hyundai, Korea (SS 12/2026, DD 01/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold back in June at USD 32,5 mill. The Kamsarmax \"Hellenic C\" 81/2014 Jiangsu, China (SS 09/2029, DD 10/2027, BWTS fitted) of Cosmoship Management was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 21 mill. For reference, the two-years-older sister vessel \"Nova Optimus\" 81/2012 Jiangsu, China (SS 09/2027, DD 12/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold back in October at USD 16,5 mill. On the Supramax sector, Neptune Lines Shipping committed their \"ND Armonia\" 56/2011 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 09/2025, BWTS fitted) to Far Eastern interests at region USD 18 mill. Note that the sister vessel \"Nordic Stavanger\" 56/2011 Mitsui, Japan (SS 11/2026, DD 12/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold back in July at the same levels. Moreover, the \"Lista\" 55/2011 IHI, Japan (SS/DD 01/2027, BWTS fitted) was committed to clients of VOSCO at mid USD 16 mill, while the one-year-older sister vessel \"Nordic BC Kiel\" 56/2010 IHI, Japan (SS/DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD High USD 14 mill. Following the sales of the Handysize \"Four Aida\" 34/2009 Spp, Korea (SS 09/2029, DD 02/2026, BWTS fitted) & \"Four Otello\" 34/2010 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) at USD 23 mill enbloc, Premuda SpA committed their sister vessel \"Four Nabucco\" 34/2010 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) at USD 11,8 mill. In addition, the OHBS \"Aegean Spire\" 33/2008 Shin Kochi, Japan (SS/DD 09/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed at USD 11,8 mill also. Note that the sister vessel \"Elegant Emilie\" 33/2008 Shin Kochi, Japan (SS/DD 09/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold in September at USD 12,5 mill.",
    "tankers": "Maran Tankers committed their VLCC \"Maran Aries\" 320/2006 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 10/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) to Chinese interests at region USD 45,5 mill. Remind you that the one-year-younger \"Gesi\" 305/2007 Daewoo, Korea (SS 03/2027, DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 43,25 mill. The Suezmax \"Evagoras\" 165/2003 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS 03/2028, DD 06/2026, BWTS fitted) was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 25 mill. For reference, the two-years-younger \"Jag Lalit\" 158/2005 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS 07/2028, DD 04/2026, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1B) was sold back in September at region USD 33 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 7,000/9,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 9,000/11,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 8,000/9,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 10,000/11,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via US Gulf were fixed around usd 8,000/10,000 pd. Continental trips via US Gulf into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. South American trips into China were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 300K/500K. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 11,600 pd for 10/12 months employment basis delivery West Coast India.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of trips from China into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Indonesian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 11,000/13,000 pd. Indian coastal trips were fixed around usd 12,000 pd. Indian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 7,000/10,000 pd. South African trips into India were fixed around usd 15,000/16,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 150K/160K. Mediterranean trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 7,000/8,000 pd. Mediterranean trips into North Coast South America were fixed around usd 6,000/8,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of Mediterranean trips into Continent were fixed around usd 7,000/8,000 pd. Continental trips into US East Coast were reported at the level of usd 9,000/12,000 pd. South American trips into Continent or West Africa were fixed around usd 11,000/14,000 pd. South American coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 12,000/15,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
